    "body": "\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nCloses #41230.\r\n\r\nDocument the aggregation semantics for NIXL KV connector metrics across\r\nmultiple vLLM workers.\r\n\r\nThis documentation explains that:\r\n- NIXL KV transfer statistics are collected independently by each worker.\r\n- Underlying observations are combined across workers before reduction.\r\n- Average transfer time, post time, and descriptor counts are calculated\r\n  from the combined observations.\r\n- P90 transfer and post times are calculated from the combined observations.\r\n- Transfer volume and throughput are calculated using the aggregated\r\n  total bytes and transfer duration.\r\n- Transfer, handshake, and notification failures are grouped into\r\n  `Num failed transfers`.\r\n- KV expiration events are reported separately as `Num KV expired reqs`.\r\n\r\nNo production code changes are included.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n- Reviewed the existing NIXL KV connector implementation in\r\n  `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/nixl/stats.py`.\r\n- Reviewed the existing NIXL KV connector aggregation tests.\r\n- Verified that the documentation matches the current `aggregate()` and\r\n  `reduce()` implementations.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\r\n- Documentation-only change; no production test suite changes required.\r\n- No production code was modified.\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [x] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [x] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [x] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>",
